      "writtenOn": "2026-07-27T23:30:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Ah, yeah, however `ConvolveVerticalPass` requires the template parameters to be compile time constants, so they have to be wrapped and passed and then unwrapped in the lambda.\n\u003e \n\u003e To avoid them I can restore to calling `ConvolveVerticalPass` directly but that has a bit more code duplications.\n\u003e \n\u003e Which do you think is the better approach?\n\nCan you give an example in the comments here? I think a lambda should work with a constant value, but there are a few layers of expansion here, so it\u0027s hard to see what\u0027s going on.",
      "parentUuid": "aea4d5fc_35ef9bac",
      "revId": "0f880bd0cc4373e5b8e138455dddbf90017b1c15",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
    {
