      "writtenOn": "2026-07-28T14:45:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It basically boils down to the template parameters of `ConvolveVerticalPass` are non-type, so when calling it, those have to be compile time constants. But lambda arguments are all run-time variables, so they need to be wrapped...\n\nFor example, `dispatch_h_skip_lim` calls `invoke` with one argument `taps_y_const` so it is wrapped here, and then `invoke` adds a few more when calling `ConvolveVerticalPass`, and those are wrapped there.\n\nGiven the multi-layer expansion, maybe it is a good idea to get rid of these lambdas?...",
      "parentUuid": "c90f4887_864f2d58",
      "revId": "0f880bd0cc4373e5b8e138455dddbf90017b1c15",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
